# Chained kans: open kan, replacement draw, added kan, discard, ron
# (engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5 items 4 & 10).
# Setup: Seat 0 discards 9p -> Seat 1 pons 9p (using 99p), discards 1s.
# Seats 2, 3 tsumogiri; Seat 0 draws 2z, discards 5z -> Seat 1 calls daiminkan on 5z
# (owes kan dora #1: 1p -> dora 2p), draws rinshan[0] (4th 9p), declares kakan 9p!
# Robbing window passes (no robber) -> owed kan dora #1 (1p) flips BEFORE rinshan[1],
# and kakan 9p owes kan dora #2 (7p -> dora 8p).
# Seat 1 draws rinshan[1] (7s), discards 7s -> Seat 2 rons 7s (holding one 2p and two 8p!).
# Scoring for Seat 2 (non-dealer, West):
#   Hand: 234m 678m 234p 56s 88p + ron 7s
#   - Mahjong Soul (default): kan dora #1 (1p -> 2p, +1) IS active; kan dora #2 (7p -> 8p) is NOT:
#     pinfu (1) + tanyao (1) + dora:1 (2p) = 3 han 30 fu -> 3900 from Seat 1.
#   - Tenhou: BOTH kan dora #1 (2p, +1) and kan dora #2 (88p, +2, flipped before the discard) ARE active:
#     pinfu (1) + tanyao (1) + dora:3 = 5 han (Mangan) -> 8000 from Seat 1.

[meta]
name: open_kan_chained_kan_discard_ron
title: Open kan -> replacement draw -> added kan -> discard -> ron (owed dora ordering)
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5.4, §5.10
unverified: rules.md §5 items 4 and 10 (Mahjong Soul chained kan dora and post-kan ron)

[round]
wind: E
round: 1
honba: 0
sticks: 0
dealer: 0
scores: 25000 25000 25000 25000

[wall]
hand 0: 9p 5z 111p 111s 999s 1m 9m
hand 1: 99p 555z 1s 1199m 556p
hand 2: 234m 678m 234p 56s 88p
hand 3: 3344m 6677p 3344s 6z
dora: 3z 1p 7p
rinshan: 9p 7s
draws: 4z 4z 4z 2z

[steps]
0 discard 9p
window: 1=pon:99p
1 discard 1s
window: 0=pass
2 tsumogiri 4z
3 tsumogiri 4z
0 discard 5z
window: 1=daiminkan
1 kakan 9p
1 tsumogiri 7s
window: 2=ron

